## Analysis

**Valid modulus measurements (with fit quality context):**
| Experiment | Modulus (MPa) | CV | Fit Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 17.5wt%, 65°C, 6mm/s, N2, 15s, 10°C bath, 1800s | **708.9** | 0.129 | No discarded score reported |
| 17.5wt%, 55°C, 11mm/s, N2, 375s, 25°C bath, 1300s | 591.7 | 0.109 | 54.5/100 |
| 17wt%, 35°C, 8mm/s, N2, 0s, 5°C bath, 1200s | 569.3 | 0.046 | 60/100 |
| 17wt%, 25°C, 10mm/s, N2, 30s, 5°C bath, 1200s | 547.2 | 0.112 | 58/100 |
| 17.5wt%, 25°C, 9mm/s, N2, 120s, 25°C bath, 1800s | 494.6 | 0.176 | 26.5/100 |
| 19wt%, 65°C, 2mm/s, N2, 30s, 15°C bath, 1600s | 491.1 | 0.091 | 62/100 |
| 18wt%, 80°C, 15mm/s, NoN2, 600s, 15°C bath, 1350s | 476.8 | 0.091 | 0/100 |
| 17.5wt%, 65°C, 6mm/s, N2, 15s, 10°C bath, 1800s (run2) | 474.7 | nan | 39.7/100 |

**Key observations:**
- Best validated modulus: 708.9 MPa (17.5wt%, 65°C, 6mm/s, N2, 15s, 10°C, 1800s) — but run2 at same conditions gave only 474.7 MPa with poor fit quality. This is a large discrepancy; the run2 had 3 failed fits. The first run had no discarded fit score reported (all fits passed), making it the more reliable measurement. The repeat did not confirm the high value — this candidate is not yet validated.

**However**, the validation policy says to prioritize a repeat when an apparent best candidate has not been independently reproduced with a large apparent gain. The run2 IS an independent repeat, but it gave a much lower value with poor fit quality. This is inconclusive — not a confirmed improvement, not a confirmed failure. A third independent repeat would resolve this.

**But the mode is EXPLORE**, not validate. The instruction says "Allow an exact repeat when a promising candidate needs independent validation under the validation policy." The 708.9 MPa candidate has one repeat that was inconclusive (poor fit quality in run2). Given explore mode, I should prioritize novel coverage.

**Design space gaps:**
- `bath_temp`: 5, 10, 15, 20, 25°C covered — all 5 values sampled
- `mixing_temp`: 25–80 covered but sparse at ~25–35 range with higher polymer_wt
- `polymer_wt`: 17–21 covered; 17–17.5 range dominates the successful modulus results
- `pullcast_speed`: 1–20 covered broadly
- `coupon_to_bath_wait_time`: 0–600 covered; mid-range (200–350s) with N2+low bath temp is sparse
- `nips_bath_wait_time`: 1200–1800 covered; 1200s with low bath temp + N2 + ~17wt% is a sparse combination
- Notably: **low polymer_wt (~17–17.5) + cold bath (5°C) + N2 + moderate mixing temp + moderate-high pullcast speed** seems promising but underexplored with varied wait times

**Novel region to explore:**
- polymer_wt ~18.0 (moderate, between the dense 17–17.5 cluster and higher wt%)
- mixing_temp ~25°C (low end, underrepresented with 18wt%)
- bath_temp = 5°C (cold bath associated with better modulus)
- pullcast_speed ~17 mm/s (high speed, sparse in cold-bath+N2 region)
- coupon_to_bath_wait_time ~270s (mid-range, sparse for N2+cold bath)
- nips_bath_wait_time ~1700s (long, sparse for this combination)
- nitrogen = True

This combination is genuinely novel — no experiment has combined 18wt% + 25°C mixing + 5°C bath + high pullcast + N2 + mid wait time.

