## Analysis

**Validated modulus results (with measured Elastic Modulus):**
| Experiment | polymer_wt | mixing_temp | bath_temp | pullcast_speed | N₂ | wait_time | nips_time | E (MPa) | CV |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 17wt, 25°C, 5°C bath, 10mm/s, N₂, 30s, 1200s | 17 | 25 | 5 | 10 | T | 30 | 1200 | 547 | 0.112 |
| 18wt, 80°C, 15°C bath, 15mm/s, NoN₂, 600s, 1350s | 18 | 80 | 15 | 15 | F | 600 | 1350 | 477 | 0.091 |
| 17wt, 35°C, 10°C bath, 20mm/s, NoN₂, 90s, 1400s | 17 | 35 | 10 | 20 | F | 90 | 1400 | 401 | 0.012 |
| 17.5wt, 55°C, 25°C bath, 11mm/s, N₂, 375s, 1300s | 17.5 | 55 | 25 | 11 | T | 375 | 1300 | **592** | 0.109 |
| 18wt, 30°C, 20°C bath, 16mm/s, N₂, 500s, 1450s | 18 | 30 | 20 | 16 | T | 500 | 1450 | 400 | nan |
| 17.5wt, 25°C, 25°C bath, 9mm/s, N₂, 120s, 1800s | 17.5 | 25 | 25 | 9 | T | 120 | 1800 | 495 | 0.176 |
| 17.5wt, 65°C, 10°C bath, 6mm/s, N₂, 15s, 1800s | 17.5 | 65 | 10 | 6 | T | 15 | 1800 | **709** | 0.129 |
| 17.5wt, 75°C, 10°C bath, 14mm/s, N₂, 45s, 1550s | 17.5 | 75 | 10 | 14 | T | 45 | 1550 | 210 | nan |
| 19wt, 65°C, 15°C bath, 2mm/s, N₂, 30s, 1600s | 19 | 65 | 15 | 2 | T | 30 | 1600 | 491 | 0.091 |
| 17wt, 35°C, 5°C bath, 8mm/s, N₂, 0s, 1200s | 17 | 35 | 5 | 8 | T | 0 | 1200 | 569 | 0.046 |
| 17.5wt, 65°C, 10°C bath, 6mm/s, N₂, 15s, 1800s (run2) | 17.5 | 65 | 10 | 6 | T | 15 | 1800 | 475 | nan |
| 18.5wt, 25°C, 5°C bath, 19mm/s, NoN₂, 330s, 1800s | 18.5 | 25 | 5 | 19 | F | 330 | 1800 | 667 | nan |

**Key observations:**
- Best single measurement: 17.5wt/65°C/10°C/6mm/s/N₂/15s/1800s → 709 MPa (run1), but run2 gave 475 MPa — high variability between independent repeats, not confirmed.
- Second best: 18.5wt/25°C/5°C/19mm/s/NoN₂/330s/1800s → 667 MPa (single measurement, no repeat, CV=nan, fit quality 37/100 with 3 discarded).
- Third: 17.5wt/55°C/25°C/11mm/s/N₂/375s/1300s → 592 MPa.

**Explore mode — design space coverage:**

Looking at sparse regions:
- **bath_temp**: 5°C and 10°C are heavily sampled; 15°C has 2 points; 20°C has 2 points; 25°C has 3 points. Bath temp of 5°C is very dense.
- **polymer_wt**: 17–17.5 heavily sampled; 18–19 moderate; 19.5–21 sparse with no valid modulus.
- **mixing_temp**: 25°C (4 pts), 35°C (2), 40°C, 45°C, 50°C, 55°C, 60°C, 65°C (3), 70°C, 75°C, 80°C — fairly well covered.
- **coupon_to_bath_wait_time**: 0, 15, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120, 150, 225, 270, 300, 330, 375, 450, 500, 600 — very well covered. Missing: ~540s range.
- **nips_bath_wait_time**: 1200 (3), 1250, 1300, 1350, 1400, 1450, 1500, 1550, 1600, 1650, 1700, 1750, 1800 (4) — well covered.
- **pullcast_speed**: 1–20 all unique, well covered.
- **nitrogen**: 12 True, 6 False — reasonably balanced.

**Sparse/underrepresented regions:**
- Higher polymer_wt (19–21) with bath_temp in the 15–20°C range and mixing_temp in the 40–55°C range — most high-wt experiments used bath_temp=5°C.
- polymer_wt ~20–21 with valid modulus: none (21wt failed completely; 20wt and 20.5wt had all fits discarded).
- A combination of higher polymer_wt (~20wt), intermediate bath_temp (~15°C), moderate mixing_temp (~50°C), and intermediate wait time is unexplored.

**Proposed experiment:**
- polymer_wt = 20.0 (sparse region for valid modulus)
- mixing_temp = 50°C (feasible for 20wt; distinct from 45°C used before)
- bath_temp = 15°C (underrepresented for high polymer_wt)
- pullcast_speed = 12 mm/s (unused speed)
- nitrogen = False (adds diversity; high-wt experiments mostly used N₂ or ambient)
- coupon_to_bath_wait_time = 540 s (near max, sparse)
- nips_bath_wait_time = 1450 s (mid-range)
- additive_wt = 0

This combination is genuinely novel: high polymer_wt with warm bath, long wait, no N₂, mid mixing temp — far from any existing point.

